  "levels": [
    {
      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Commissions and fees",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Commissions and fees"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-prowizje-i-oplaty.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fees **reduce your profit** every time – whether the market rises or falls. The two most important:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Brokerage commission** – paid once on every purchase and sale",
                "**TER** – the fund's annual cost, deducted automatically from its result"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Check the fees before you buy and look for cheap options, e.g. savings plans **with no commission**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Fees vs profit over the long term",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Fees vs profit over the long term"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/2-oplaty-kontra-zysk.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fees work like **compound interest in reverse**: they take not only their own amount, but also all the gains that money would have earned over the years."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Passive ETF** – about 0.2% a year",
                "**Active fund** – up to 2.0% a year"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "After 20–30 years this difference can take **as much as a third** of your capital. Low costs mean a better result **with no extra risk**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Tax on gains",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Tax on gains"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/3-podatek-od-zyskow.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You pay tax on investment gains: in Poland the **Belka tax**, in Germany the **Abgeltungsteuer**. It covers, among other things:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "gains from **selling** shares and ETFs",
                "**dividends**",
                "**interest** from deposits and bonds"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "You only pay on the **profit**, and only once you realise it. As long as you hold the investment, all your capital **keeps working**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l4",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Tax reliefs",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Tax reliefs"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/4-ulgi-podatkowe.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The state offers **legal ways** to pay less tax or none at all – in return for saving long-term, e.g. for retirement."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**IKE** (Poland) – no Belka tax when you withdraw in retirement",
                "**IKZE** (Poland) – you deduct payments from your income in your tax return",
                "**Sparer-Pauschbetrag** (Germany) – 1,000 € of gains a year tax-free"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "More profit stays in the portfolio and **drives compound interest**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
